cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If ttl3d helped your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ttl3d: a self-contained 3D and 2D HTML viewer for RDF graphs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abadifard
    given-names: Soheil
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22716060
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22716060
    description: The concept DOI, resolving to the latest release on Zenodo
repository-code: "https://github.com/soheilabadifard/TTL_to_3D"
url: "https://soheilabadifard.github.io/TTL_to_3D/"
abstract: >-
  ttl3d turns RDF into a single self-contained HTML page that shows the graph in
  3D or 2D, with labels, a legend by file, type or namespace, label search and a
  detail card for every node. It reads Turtle, N-Triples, RDF/XML, JSON-LD, TriG
  and N-Quads, several files at once with each named graph as a legend row of its
  own, or a CONSTRUCT query against a SPARQL endpoint, and it can cut a large
  graph down to a neighbourhood or to its schema before drawing it. A Python API
  shows the same page inline in Jupyter. The page embeds all of its JavaScript,
  so it opens from a file and works offline.
keywords:
  - RDF
  - Turtle
  - OWL
  - ontology
  - knowledge graph
  - semantic web
  - linked data
  - SPARQL
  - graph visualization
